# Keep the Docker build context lean. Without this file, `COPY models ...`
# pulls every directory under nlp/models/ — including the 16 GB BF16 merged
# checkpoint that v15-merged-qwen3-8b produced as a STEP-1 intermediate.
# That blows up the COPY layer to 16+ GB and makes every push to Artifact
# Registry painful.
#
# We only want the runtime artefacts inside the image:
#   - nlp/models/lora/                 — LoRA adapter (for Ampere+ runtime path)
#   - nlp/models/llm-merged/           — AWQ-quantised merged model (T4 path)
#   - nlp/models/answer_ranker.json    — historical v12 ranker
#   - nlp/models/*-finetuned-squad2/   — historical extractive QA fine-tunes
#
# Everything else is training intermediate and stays on the Workbench disk.

models/qwen3-8b-merged-bf16/
models/lora-archive/
models/*.bf16/
models/checkpoints/

# Per-run trainer state (only relevant when we accidentally save under
# nlp/models/; the real runs/ dir lives at training/nlp/runs/ which is
# already outside the nlp/ build context).
models/runs/

# HF transformers cache, just in case anyone accidentally points HF_HOME
# at nlp/models/.
models/.cache/
models/.locks/
